IMPORT prelude

§ `A record whose every field is a STRING`

-- REGRESSION EXHIBIT. R11 elides an uninspected `STRING` field from the
-- emitted structure. A record all of whose fields are strings therefore loses
-- all of them, and until 2026-09-21 the emitter printed what was left:
--
--     declaration structure Provenance:
--
--     … Finding { -- amount: claimed -- sources: [ Provenance { } ] … }
--
-- and exited 0. Catala 1.2.1 accepts neither half. Measured, both errors from
-- one `catala typecheck` run:
--
--   * "No fields defined for structure Provenance. Please define at least
--     one." — there is no spelling of an empty structure to fall back on;
--   * a syntax error at `}` in `Provenance { }` — "expected a list of field
--     bindings of the form '-- fld : expression'".
--
-- So R11's elision now carries upward: a structure that loses every field is
-- itself elided, and so is every field of another structure that carries one,
-- which is why `sources` is gone from `Finding` below. Both disclosures are in
-- the emitted notes block. Reading such a field, naming such a structure in a
-- type, or building one is a `LowerError` — the shape divergence is the cost
-- R11 already discloses, and answering a question about a field that is not
-- there would be worse.
--
-- `Finding` survives because two of its fields are not strings. The whole of
-- the citation apparatus — which document, which clause — is what Catala
-- cannot carry, and the numbers it was cited in support of are what it can.

DECLARE Provenance
    HAS document IS A STRING
        clause   IS A STRING

DECLARE Finding
    HAS amount  IS A NUMBER
        sources IS A LIST OF Provenance
        settled IS A BOOLEAN

@export What is found on a claimed amount, with the sources relied on.
GIVEN claimed IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Finding
`finding on` claimed MEANS
    Finding WITH
        amount  IS claimed TIMES 2
        sources IS LIST (Provenance WITH document IS "Terms", clause IS "cl.3")
        settled IS claimed GREATER THAN 0

@export The amount found, without the apparatus that cites it.
GIVEN claimed IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`amount found on` claimed MEANS (`finding on` claimed)'s amount

-- The whole `Finding` has no Catala JSON rendering — `sources` is not in the
-- emitted structure, so L4's value and Catala's are different shapes and R7
-- declines to write an expected block rather than write a wrong one. The note
-- saying so sits in the run's stderr. The second directive is testable, and is
-- here so this exhibit contributes a live `clerk test` case rather than only a
-- golden.
#EVAL `finding on` 50

#EVAL `amount found on` 50
